2752..2827 Comment "/// Spinning undoes winding at every word: the round trip at a variable, by"
2828..2902 Comment "/// induction over the presented words. The result type reads the word the"
2903..2974 Comment "/// fold descends on, so each arm answers it at its constructor and the"
2975..3033 Comment "/// recursive call at the field: `sectWords[<](x)` relates"
3034..3109 Comment "/// `spinWords(windWords(x))` to `x`, and carried along `around` it relates"
3110..3184 Comment "/// `Loop(spinWords(windWords(x)))`, which `spinWords(windWords(Loop(x)))`"
3185..3262 Comment "/// runs to, to `Loop(x)`. The case respects both rules: at `Loop(Unloop(x))`"
3263..3337 Comment "/// the arms compose to `cong(around, cong(unaround, p))`, whose functions"
3338..3414 Comment "/// compose to the identity under the rules, so the chain is `p` itself, the"
3415..3433 Comment "/// answer at `x`."
